s, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n? Go map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and write, no newline. That changes body. Need keep same response bodies. Could use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) for success. But if user struct with fields Name, Email", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0035596590023487806], [760, -6.753326892852783]], [[1144, -1.1563368389033712e-05], [14235, -12.023506164550781]], [[4087, -0.011713654734194279], [310, -4.649799823760986]], [[1156, -0.03475606068968773], [303, -3.5873777866363525]], [[579, -0.22529146075248718], [25, -2.358721971511841]], [[1622, -0.003153343452140689], [3296, -6.54094934463501]], [[13, -0.3455195724964142], [25, -1.5870890617370605]], [[14235, -0.03547724708914757], [1165, -4.071701526641846]], [[89109, -0.3367416262626648], [7936, -1.7955313920974731]], [[5805, -0.0002590157091617584], [2400, -8.639995574951172]], [[9830, -0.026105791330337524], [6795, -3.7083852291107178]], [[6795, -2.8849064619862475e-05], [17369, -11.94424057006836]], [[1083, -1.3798632621765137], [47781, -1.6059298515319824]], [[1228, -0.09829618036746979], [2400, -2.7697324752807617]], [[470, -3.302151890238747e-05], [5568, -10.60377025604248]], [[5568, -0.002906967420130968], [74243, -6.1645660400390625]], [[440, -0.9144571423530579], [25, -1.8835657835006714]], [[2708, -0.0356430783867836], [181